isolate_push_fanout_failures.s:
THE primary root cause, proven live: ws/src/hub.ts send_push_notification (lines 329-366) fans out to every stored subscription with `await Promise.all([...subs.entries()].map(async ([key, sub]) => { const r = await send_push(...); if (r.gone) gone.push(key); }))` and NO per-subscription error handling. The first rejection (e.g. `DataError: Failed to import raw EC key data: Invalid point encoding` from a corrupt p256dh — observed in production via `wrangler tail x2-ws` as `[RELAY] uid=cedab23a-... DO fetch THREW: DataError: Failed to import raw EC key data: Invalid point encoding.`) rejects the whole Promise.all, so send_push_notification throws, which propagates out of the /relay handler's `await this.send_push_notification(...)` (hub.ts:77), making the recipient's ChatHub /relay fetch throw. Result: NOT ONE device of that user receives a push — one corrupt subscription (or one oversized message) silently bricks all notifications for the account. (The demo: register a sub with a random non-0x04 65-byte p256dh for a test account, send a message to it, watch `[RELAY] DO fetch THREW` and zero pushes; swap in a valid key and the relay succeeds.)

Fix in TWO places in ws/src/hub.ts:

(1) The fan-out (current lines 353-365):
```ts
		const gone: string[] = [];
		await Promise.all(
			[...subs.entries()].map(async ([key, sub]) => {
				const r = await send_push(
					{ endpoint: sub.ep, keys: { p256dh: sub.k, auth: sub.au } },
					payload,
					keys,
					opts
				);
				if (r.gone) gone.push(key);
			})
		);
		if (gone.length) await this.state.storage.delete(gone);
```
becomes:
```ts
		const gone: string[] = [];
		await Promise.all(
			[...subs.entries()].map(async ([key, sub]) => {
				try {
					const r = await send_push(
						{ endpoint: sub.ep, keys: { p256dh: sub.k, auth: sub.au } },
						payload,
						keys,
						opts
					);
					if (r.gone) gone.push(key);
				} catch (e) {
					// one corrupt sub must not silence the other devices — log and prune it
					console.error(`[HUB-PUSH] sub ${key} failed — pruning:`, e);
					gone.push(key);
				}
			})
		);
		if (gone.length) await this.state.storage.delete(gone);
```

(2) The /relay handler (current lines 74-89) — a push failure must never throw out of relay; message delivery and unread already happened above it:
```ts
			const delivered = this.deliver(to, payload);
