dev_vapid_parity_and_diagnostics.s:
Fifth root cause: ws/src/hub.ts send_push_notification reads VAPID with NO fallback — `const pub = await get_secret(this.env.VAPID_PUBLIC);` etc. (lines 340-342) — then `if (!pub || !priv || !subject) return;` (line 343). In local dev the ws worker's Secrets Store is empty (the local store 45748cb1c67946df943075fa14cb8815 holds only MESSAGE_ENC_KEY/TURN_KEY_*/X2_ORIGIN) and ws/.env has no VAPID values, so every dev push silently no-ops with zero signal. In production the remote store HAS all three (verified: GET /api/push -> 200 with a key) so this is a dev-experience/diagnosability fix, but it makes the missing-keys path loud instead of a silent return.

Changes:
